Reduce backdrop blur while the user scrolls fast. Heavy blur during motion destroys perceived smoothness and increases GPU workload. Lowering blur dynamically keeps interfaces crisp while also improving performance.

``javascript
let t;

const nav = document.querySelector(".navbar");
window.addEventListener("scroll", () => {
	nav.style.backdropFilter = "blur(8px)";
	clearTimeout(t);

	t = setTimeout(() => {
		nav.style.backdropFilter = "blur(24px)";
	}, 120);
});
``

``css
scrollbar-width: thin;
scrollbar-color: gray transparent;
``
